1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:01,719
A queen crossed a desert to test

2
00:00:01,779 --> 00:00:02,859
if a rumor was true.

3
00:00:03,919 --> 00:00:05,779
She had heard about Solomon's wisdom and

4
00:00:05,799 --> 00:00:06,559
did not believe it.

5
00:00:07,659 --> 00:00:09,840
So she came herself, with hard questions,

6
00:00:10,079 --> 00:00:11,099
to see for herself.

7
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,239
She said it plainly:

8
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,960
"It was a true report that I

9
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:17,639
heard in mine own land of thy

10
00:00:17,739 --> 00:00:19,079
acts and of thy wisdom.

11
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:23,219
Howbeit I believed not the words, until

12
00:00:23,319 --> 00:00:25,699
I came, and mine eyes had seen

13
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:25,959
it:

14
00:00:26,719 --> 00:00:29,279
and, behold, the half was not told

15
00:00:29,379 --> 00:00:30,979
me." She had doubted a report.

16
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,179
Seeing it changed everything.

17
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,880
Centuries later, Jesus pointed straight back

18
00:00:36,959 --> 00:00:38,599
to her, to make a claim about

19
00:00:38,639 --> 00:00:39,219
Himself:

20
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:41,239
"The queen of the south shall rise

21
00:00:41,299 --> 00:00:43,299
up in the judgment with this generation...

22
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:45,680
for she came from the uttermost parts

23
00:00:45,719 --> 00:00:47,039
of the earth to hear the wisdom

24
00:00:47,079 --> 00:00:47,700
of Solomon;

25
00:00:48,459 --> 00:00:51,099
and, behold, a greater than Solomon is

26
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:54,360
here." She crossed a continent to verify

27
00:00:54,439 --> 00:00:55,340
a king's wisdom.

28
00:00:56,439 --> 00:00:58,079
A greater than Solomon is already in

29
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:58,579
front of you.

30
00:00:59,299 --> 00:01:00,680
You do not have to travel anywhere

31
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:01,979
to find out if it is true.

32
00:01:03,299 --> 00:01:04,979
Just ask Him your hardest question.
